# Single source of truth for valid TODO/FIXME Linear issue references.
# Every `// TODO(APP-N)` or `// FIXME(APP-N)` in source MUST cite one of these
# verified-open issue IDs. The Spotless `EnforceLinearTicketTodos` custom step
# reads this file at build time and fails the build on any TODO citing a
# closed, non-existent, or self-referential (current PR's parent) ID, or any
# placeholder shape (<linear-id>, <issue-id>, APP-NNN, APP-???-X, "Issue X").
#
# Each ID was verified open against live Linear state during Phase 3 plan
# preparation. Done IDs (APP-31, APP-37, APP-60, APP-242, etc.) are
# deliberately excluded — a TODO citing a Done ticket fails the lint because
# "Done" means no further work is happening on that ticket.
#
# Format: one ID per line; lines starting with `#` are comments; blank lines
# ignored. The Spotless step strips comments + whitespace before matching.
#
